  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Georgia",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1f38f221fe87c9c3bffdfe6e0148ceaa3b4c2edbb25d4b4b870852f3dd79643f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1f38f221fe87-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Georgia, for some 6 decades now, the policy of the United States has been to embrace integration, reject segregation and separation of people. We stand -- really, the Nation of the United States of America stands pretty much as the beacon in the world to the notion that balkanization is not the way to go."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Walbert (State)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1f38f221fe87c9c3bffdfe6e0148ceaa3b4c2edbb25d4b4b870852f3dd79643f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1f38f221fe87-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Walbert (State), according to Mr. Walbert (State), the ends of Congress must be legitimate and the ends must be related proportionately and with congruence, the -- the remedies that are chosen by Congress. And I would have to say what is -- other than just preserving what happens to be there -- the only reason we're talking about keeping safe seats is they happen to be there. This is not because they're ever put in because of a remedy."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Walbert",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1f38f221fe87c9c3bffdfe6e0148ceaa3b4c2edbb25d4b4b870852f3dd79643f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1f38f221fe87-0003-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Walbert, we have 4 congressmen out of 13 who are African American, 52 percent district, 50 percent district, 41 percent district, and 38 percent district. Last one just elected 13 -- Congressional District 13 just created -- this reapportionment got two new districts. 13 was open, 38 percent, African American elected. African American elected in the last election in a 28 percent multi-member house district. It's working."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Walbert",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1f38f221fe87c9c3bffdfe6e0148ceaa3b4c2edbb25d4b4b870852f3dd79643f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1f38f221fe87-0003-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Walbert, there is oral argument next week on that, Your Honor, and we expect that to be decided very quickly."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Walbert",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1f38f221fe87c9c3bffdfe6e0148ceaa3b4c2edbb25d4b4b870852f3dd79643f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1f38f221fe87-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Walbert, it would be a tragedy. And we're well aware of the history. We're not up here apologizing that we are disowning the history of race in Georgia. We know what it is. The Attorney General knows what it is. But it would be a tragedy on the facts of this case to utilize that history to penalize what African Americans are trying to do ... Integration's working in Georgia."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Georgia (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
